-- title:
--   Supersingular places of the level-one j-line are the supersingular points
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a natural number and $K$ a field, and let $F_1 =$ `modularFunctionFieldC K 1` be the $K$-subfield of the Laurent series field $K((X))$ generated by the $q$-expansion $j$-series `jqModC K` (the Laurent series $X^{-1}$ times the reduction to $K$ of the integral power series `jNum`) together with `jqNModC K 1`. Let $w$ be a place of $F_1$ over $K$, i.e. a valuation subring of $F_1$ which contains the image of $K$, is not all of $F_1$, and is a principal ideal ring. The theorem asserts the equivalence of two conditions on $w$. First, $w$ lies in `ssPlaces q 1 K`, that is: $w$ satisfies `Place.IsRational`, $w$ satisfies `IsAffineGeomPlace K 1`, and the residue value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen K 1)` of the moduli generator at $w$ lies in `ssJSet q K`, the set of those $a \in K$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $K$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$. Second, there exists $a \in$ `ssJSet q K` with $w =$ `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint K a`, the place obtained by transporting the finite place of $K(X)$ attached to $X - C\,a$ along the $K$-algebra isomorphism `ratFuncEquivCharLOneC K` from $K(X)$ to $F_1$.
--
--   This identifies the supersingular locus on the level-one geometric modular curve with the finite set of places of the $j$-line centred at the supersingular $j$-invariants, in the form used when the modular curve is compared with quaternionic data. It is cited in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison of the supersingular places with a class set, and in the analysis of the Deligne–Rapoport model around the nodes.
